hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17302","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Abu Khalaf Musa ibn Khalaf, who was counted among the Budala, haddathana Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from his grandfather Mamtur, from al-Harith al-Ashari, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Exalted is He, commanded Yahya ibn Zakariyya (peace be upon them) with five words, to act upon them and to command Banu Israil to act upon them, and he was about to delay, so Isa said to him: You have been commanded with five words, to act upon them and to command Banu Israil to act upon them, so either you convey them or I convey them. He said: O my brother, I fear that if you precede me I will be punished or swallowed up. He said: So Yahya gathered Banu Israil in Bayt al-Maqdis until the mosque was filled, and he sat upon the balconies, then he praised Allah and extolled Him, then he said: Allah, Exalted is He, commanded me with five words, to act upon them and to command you to act upon them. The first of them is to worship Allah and not associate anything with Him, for the likeness of that is the likeness of a man who bought a slave with his pure wealth, with silver or gold, and he worked and gave his yield to other than his master, so which of you would like his slave to be like that. And Allah, Exalted is He, created you and provided for you, so worship Him and do not associate anything with Him. And I command you with prayer, for Allah, Exalted is He, sets His face toward the face of His servant so long as he does not turn aside, so when you pray do not turn aside. And I command you with fasting, for the likeness of that is the likeness of a man with a purse of musk among a group, all of them smelling the scent of musk, and the breath of the fasting person with Allah is more pleasant than the scent of musk. And I command you with charity, for the likeness of that is the likeness of a man whom the enemy captured and tied his hands to his neck and brought him forward to strike his neck, and he said: Will you let me ransom myself from you, so he ransomed himself from them with little and much until he freed himself. And I command you with much remembrance of Allah, Exalted is He, and the likeness of that is the likeness of a man whom the enemy pursued swiftly in his tracks, and he came to a fortified fortress and fortified himself in it, and the servant is most protected from Satan when he is in remembrance of Allah, Exalted is He. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And I command you with five, Allah commanded me with them: with the community, and hearing, and obedience, and emigration, and striving in the path of Allah, for whoever leaves the community a handspan has cast off the bond of Islam from his neck unless he returns, and whoever calls with the call of ignorance is from the heap of Hell. They said: O Messenger of Allah, even if he fasts and prays. He said: Even if he fasts and prays and claims he is a Muslim, so call the Muslims by their names, by what Allah, Exalted is He, named them: the Muslims, the believers, servants of Allah, Exalted is He."
"17953","Affan narrated to us, Abu Khalaf Musa ibn Khalaf, who was counted among the Budala, narrated to us, he said, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from his grandfather Mamtour, from al-Harith al-Ashari, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Allah Almighty commanded Yahya ibn Zakariyya with five words, to act upon them and to order the Children of Israel to act upon them. He almost delayed, so Isa said to him, You have been commanded with five words, to act upon them and to order the Children of Israel to act upon them, so either you convey them or I convey them. So he said to him, O my brother, I fear if you precede me that I will be punished or swallowed up. He said, So Yahya gathered the Children of Israel in Bayt al-Maqdis until the mosque was full and they sat on the terraces. Then he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, Allah Almighty commanded me with five words, to act upon them and order you to act upon them. The first of them is to worship Allah and not associate anything with Him, for the likeness of that is like a man who buys a servant from his own pure wealth with silver or gold, and he works and gives his work to other than his master; which of you would like his servant to be so. And Allah Almighty created you and provided for you, so worship Him and do not associate anything with Him. And He commanded you with prayer, for Allah Almighty turns His face to the face of His servant so long as he does not turn away; when you pray do not turn away. And He commanded you with fasting, for the likeness of that is like a man with a pouch of musk in a company, all finding the scent of musk, and the changed breath of the fasting mouth is sweeter with Allah than the scent of musk. And He commanded you with charity, for the likeness of that is like a man captured by the enemy, they tie his hands to his neck and bring him forward to strike his neck, so he says, Will you let me ransom myself from you. So he ransoms himself from them with little and much until he frees himself. And He commanded you with much remembrance of Allah, and the likeness of that is like a man pursued swiftly by the enemy, and he comes to a fortified fortress and fortifies himself in it. And the servant is most protected from Satan when he is in remembrance of Allah Almighty. He said, And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, I command you with five things Allah commanded me with: unity, hearing, obedience, emigration, and striving in the path of Allah. For whoever leaves the community a span has cast off the yoke of Islam from his neck until he returns. And whoever calls with the call of pre-Islamic ignorance is of the embers of Hell. They said, O Messenger of Allah, though he fast and pray. He said, Though he fast and pray and claim he is a Muslim. So call the Muslims by what Allah named them: the Muslims, the believers, the servants of Allah Almighty."
